{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455716-lineage-of-vtmb-malkavian-protagonist","id":1455716,"title":"Lineage of VTMB Malkavian protagonist","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-07-28T09:53:39-07:00","id":1455716,"title":"Lineage of VTMB Malkavian protagonist","content":"<span style=\"color:#878A8C\"><span style=\"font-family:IBMPlexSans\"><span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">How do you think, which famous Malkavian could be the ancestor of the protagonist of VTMB? Petaniqua? Theophana? Camilla Banes? </span></span></span></span></span>Dev/Null? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3792,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","user":"trueann","date":". 08-01-2021, 04:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3792-trueann","name":"trueann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3792_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T11:02:30-07:00","id":1455720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>trueann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455716-lineage-of-vtmb-malkavian-protagonist#post1455716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#878A8C\"><span style=\"font-family:IBMPlexSans\"> <span style=\"color:#1A1A1B\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"> How do you think, which famous Malkavian could be the ancestor of the protagonist of VTMB? Petaniqua? Theophana? Camilla Banes?</span></span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jeanette_Voerman\" target=\"_blank\">Jeanette</a>/<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Therese_Voerman\" target=\"_blank\">Therese </a>Voerman, Baroness of Santa Monica, childe of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Jacob_(Malkavian)\" target=\"_blank\">Esau/Jacob</a>, probable author of <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Book_of_the_Grave-War\" target=\"_blank\">Das Buch vom Grabkrieg</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T12:14:21-07:00","id":1455727,"title":"","content":"Jeanette/Therese as a grandsire is a fairly logical choice. The PC's sire is an Anarch according to Strauss, Jeanette's also an Anarch already in the area, and the protagonist is pretty low generation by V20 rules. <br /> <br /> I figure Jacob/Esau is a childe of Lamdiel, as another ancient Malkavian active in the Middle East. (Don't remember where I'm getting that Lamdiel was in the Middle East, though.)<br /> <br /> I'm also fond of Tremere PCs. I like the idea that PC's sire is a younger childe of Marissa, who fled west after Vitel seized power in D.C., or perhaps a childe of that childe. Also explains the low generation and Anarch status of the sire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T16:19:08-07:00","id":1455733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>False Epiphany</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455716-lineage-of-vtmb-malkavian-protagonist?p=1455727#post1455727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm also fond of Tremere PCs. I like the idea that PC's sire is a younger childe of Marissa, who fled west after Vitel seized power in D.C., or perhaps a childe of that childe. Also explains the low generation and Anarch status of the sire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, maybe Nicolai making a second Erichto style impulse/passion embrace for Tremere sire.<br /> <br /> <br /> As an aside, something i always miss in canon versions of LA is the appearance Kevin Jackson's 9th gen childer siblings as leaders among the Bloods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-28-2021, 07:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T16:52:08-07:00","id":1455736,"title":"","content":"Funny, I've heard the theories - fan speculatin, admittedly - that the PC in Bloodlines is such low generation because Caine was covertly lowering their generation over the course of the game. Because it's highly probable he has that ability.<br /> <br /> The other theory I've heard is that the PC Diablerizes multiple vampires over the course of the game, not knowing it's forbidden. But I'm not as fond of this theory, for multiple reasons. First, the game would have made a big damn deal about the character performing Diablerie if that was the case, including things like cutscenes of them feeding, and other characters talking about Diablerie. If this was the intent, the game would have commented on it. Second, vampires who commit Diablerie would stand out to any vampire with Auspex (so it should make the character a pariah to any Toreador or Tremere character). Third, it would be kind of scummy if the game gave the players all these moral choices, but deprived them of the choice NOT to commit Diablerie.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think the PC's generation is unlikely to be a result of Diablerie. Or at the very least, it wasn't remotely the intent of the designers.<br /> <br /> Mainly I bring up these theories to suggest that we only ASSUME the PC was sired by a low generation vampire. Rather than starting high, and lowering through some artificial means.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T17:41:52-07:00","id":1455737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455716-lineage-of-vtmb-malkavian-protagonist?p=1455736#post1455736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, I've heard the theories - fan speculatin, admittedly - that the PC in Bloodlines is such low generation because Caine was covertly lowering their generation over the course of the game. Because it's highly probable he has that ability.<br /> <br /> The other theory I've heard is that the PC Diablerizes multiple vampires over the course of the game, not knowing it's forbidden. But I'm not as fond of this theory, for multiple reasons. First, the game would have made a big damn deal about the character performing Diablerie if that was the case, including things like cutscenes of them feeding, and other characters talking about Diablerie. If this was the intent, the game would have commented on it. Second, vampires who commit Diablerie would stand out to any vampire with Auspex (so it should make the character a pariah to any Toreador or Tremere character). Third, it would be kind of scummy if the game gave the players all these moral choices, but deprived them of the choice NOT to commit Diablerie.<br /> <br /> All in all, I think the PC's generation is unlikely to be a result of Diablerie. Or at the very least, it wasn't remotely the intent of the designers.<br /> <br /> Mainly I bring up these theories to suggest that we only ASSUME the PC was sired by a low generation vampire. Rather than starting high, and lowering through some artificial means.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points overall, but then i'm just jumping in the boat, one of the reasons i picked &quot;the Voerman sis are the childe of X&quot; as a springboard to adress the OP's question. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> There could be a bunch of unamed ancients or unacounted factors behind the fledgling's speedrun into badassery beside the potency of its blood, to be fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-28-2021, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T00:44:37-07:00","id":1455745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1455716-lineage-of-vtmb-malkavian-protagonist?p=1455736#post1455736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funny, I've heard the theories - fan speculatin, admittedly - that the PC in Bloodlines is such low generation because Caine was covertly lowering their generation over the course of the game. Because it's highly probable he has that ability.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't be &quot;over the course of the game&quot;, I don't remember the Fledgling's blood pool capacity changing at any point. It's the same at the moment we control them after embrace, and it's the same at the end of the game.<br /> <br /> So if Caine did it, then an ancient vampire stepped in and messed with their generation before the game started for... shits and giggles? He could, but if he did I'm put out about being 8th gen. Cut off just at the threshold of elder powers... If he's going to step in for some random kid and give them a power boost, he may as well go the whole way. Make them the newest of the 3rd or 2nd generation! <s>Literally</s> Goddamned deadbeat vampire father, ripping me off...<br /> <br /> While the Fledgling could have the merit that makes Diablerie marks invisible, it would still be odd to include it in the game without ever letting the player know.<br /> <br /> The sire being 7th gen is the least convoluted rationale of the three, especially since the Fledgling doesn't get a proper instruction on what generation is or how to lower it (if I remember right), only that thinbloods happen and the ancients are scary. Young lower generation vampires happen, and the PC starts off no resources, influence or any other background so if you were to assign them a character sheet the only background to put five dots in is generation, putting them at 8th.<br /> <br /> __________<br /> <br /> As for ancestors, I don't keep track of the big players but for some reason I like to believe that the Malk PC's &quot;ancestry&quot; comes from the Sabbat.<br /> Possibly because of Dementation. I know now the Camarilla Malks had Dementation returned to them before 2004, but for some reason I keep wondering if they could be of antitribu lineage. Especially since it seems they're seen as having a severe variant of the curse by their own clanmates.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><sup><i>Prone to hyperbole</i></sup>","edited":{"userid":26836,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","user":"Rhywbeth","date":". 07-29-2021, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26836-rhywbeth","name":"Rhywbeth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26836_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T07:42:04-07:00","id":1455753,"title":"","content":"Mind you, I also like the Gameplay and Story Integration that the PC becomes incredibly powerful regardless of age....because she does a lot of adventuring.<br /> <br /> Just like a PC that regularly games in the tabletop game.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}